# Forge IDE™

**A professional-grade computational platform built in Python.** Forge is an Octave-compatible computing environment with a modern PySide6 desktop GUI, 1,340+ built-in functions, and 29 integrated toolboxes — all open source under the Apache 2.0 license.

Forge aims to provide a free, fully-featured alternative to expensive proprietary numerical computing environments, with particular focus on students, educators, and researchers.

[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache_2.0-blue.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10%2B-green.svg)](https://python.org)
[![Tests](https://img.shields.io/badge/Tests-1%2C992_passing-brightgreen.svg)](#testing)

---

## Features

- **Octave-compatible language engine** — M-language parser and evaluator with 1-based indexing, matrix literals, cell arrays, structs, classdef OOP, and command-style syntax
- **1,340+ built-in functions** across 29 toolboxes (signal processing, linear algebra, statistics, image processing, control systems, and more)
- **PySide6 desktop GUI** with dockable panels: command window (REPL), code editor with syntax highlighting, file browser, workspace browser, plot figures, documentation viewer, and more
- **Matplotlib-powered plotting** — 2D/3D plots, subplots, figure management, zoom, pan, and export
- **MATLAB `.mat` file compatibility** via `scipy.io` for load/save interop
- **1,992 validated tests** — every function numerically verified against established reference implementations
- **Cross-platform** — runs on Windows, Linux, and macOS

## Quick Start

### Install from PyPI Mirror

**Windows (PowerShell):**
```powershell
pip install --index-url https://thecommons.cc/pypi/ --trusted-host thecommons.cc forge-ide
```

**Linux / macOS:**
```bash
pip install --index-url https://thecommons.cc/pypi/ --trusted-host thecommons.cc forge-ide
```

### Launch

```
forge
```

Or:
```
python -m forge
```

### Update

```
pip install --upgrade --no-cache-dir --index-url https://thecommons.cc/pypi/ --trusted-host thecommons.cc forge-ide
```

### Windows PATH Fix (one-time, if `forge` command not found)

```powershell
$sd = python -c "import site; print(site.getusersitepackages().replace('site-packages','Scripts'))"
[Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("PATH","$([Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('PATH','User'));$sd","User")
```

## Toolboxes

Forge ships with 29 integrated toolboxes — all included by default:

| Category | Toolbox | Functions |
|----------|---------|-----------|
| Math | Elementary Functions, Special Functions, Polynomials | 80+ |
| Linear Algebra | Core LA, Decompositions, Special Matrices | 90+ |
| Signal Processing | Filters, Windows, Transforms, Spectral Analysis | 260+ |
| Statistics & ML | Distributions, Descriptive Stats, Regression | 250+ |
| Image Processing | Filtering, Morphology, Transforms, I/O | 170+ |
| Control Systems | Transfer Functions, State-Space, Stability | 60+ |
| Optimization | Minimization, Root-Finding, Linear Programming | 30+ |
| ODE Solvers | ode45, ode23, ode15s, Event Detection | 15+ |
| Geometry | Convex Hull, Delaunay, Voronoi, Grid Data | 15+ |
| Sparse Matrices | Construction, Iterative Solvers, Eigenvalues | 30+ |
| Plotting | 2D, 3D, Handle Graphics, Export | 240+ |
| And more... | Audio, Financial, Symbolic, Communications, etc. | — |

## Architecture

```
forge/
├── app.py                 # QApplication entry point
├── gui/
│   ├── main_window.py     # MainWindow with dockable panels
│   ├── command_widget.py  # REPL / command window
│   ├── editor_widget.py   # Multi-tab code editor
│   ├── file_browser.py    # Directory tree navigator
│   ├── workspace_browser.py # Variable inspector
│   ├── plot_widget.py     # Matplotlib figure windows
│   └── ...                # Additional panels
├── engine/
│   ├── parser.py          # M-language tokenizer + AST parser
│   ├── evaluator.py       # AST execution engine
│   ├── session.py         # Workspace, path, state management
│   ├── types.py           # ForgeArray, ForgeChar, ForgeMap
│   └── builtins/          # 29 toolbox modules
└── tests/                 # 1,992 pytest tests
```

## Development

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- PySide6
- NumPy, SciPy, Matplotlib

### Install for Development

```bash
git clone https://github.com/njaxon2/the-commons-forge.git
cd the-commons-forge
pip install -e .
```

### Run Tests

```bash
pytest tests/ -x -q
```

### Run Headless (CI/VPS)

```bash
export QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen
pytest tests/ -x -q
```

